{
  "id": "sky-pool/v1",
  "about": "The Live Lab's pool of real sky samples (tools/extract_slices.py --pool). For each target, a few observations from the Breakthrough Listen Open Data Archive (the first query that finds fine-resolution files wins), or files listed directly. From each file: up to `hits` on-target hits (family stars), the strongest narrowband signals the de-Doppler search finds above `threshold` in one coarse channel (the one containing `freq_mhz`, else up to `tries` drawn at random), and `blind` blind windows (family blind-window) at seeded random frequencies in the first coarse channel read. The seed fixes every random choice, so re-running the pool cuts the same slices. TRAPPIST-1 and Epsilon Eridani were tried and left out: the archive's TRAPPIST-1 scans have only 3 time steps (a slice needs 16), and it lists no Epsilon Eridani files.",
  "seed": 20261104,
  "api": "http://seti.berkeley.edu/opendata/api",
  "threshold": 10,
  "limits": {
    "max_slices": 100,
    "max_bytes": 1500000,
    "max_targets": 8
  },
